WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.534
In your testimony, you refer

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:02.836
to private military companies

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:04.170
that Russia relies on

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.172
to undermine other nations

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:08.241
sovereignty to the extent possible

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.075
in this open setting.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.577
Can you share your perspective

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.111
on the relationship

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.545
between the Wagner Group

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:13.913
and the Russian forces

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.615
at the operational level?

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.883
And are you seeing the Wagner

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.251
Group's presence in Africa

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.187
change as a result of the war in Ukraine?

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.190
As you know,

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.092
the Wagner Group is a mercenary private

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.893
military company.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.328
They're conducting combat operations

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.397
right now in park mode, primarily

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.798
it's probably about 6000

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.266
or so actual mercenaries

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:34.100
and maybe another 20

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.135
or 30,000 recruits

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:36.469
that they get, many of whom

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.371
come from prisons,

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.774
and they are suffering an enormous amount

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.042
of casualties in the black mud area.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.610
The Ukrainians are inflicting

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.077
a lot of death

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.545
and destruction on these guys.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:48.048
In addition to Moon and Ukraine,

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:48.882
Wagner Group is in many,

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:50.116
many other places

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.285
most notably in West Africa,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.787
where they essentially have taken over

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.921
a country

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.322
and they are

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.690
they've pushed out the French out of

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.025
I think with Mali

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.193
and some other places

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:00.827
for the Wagner groups,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.828
a very aggressive group, it's

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.029
led by a very ruthless guy.

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:06.199
Prigozhin he reports to be a,

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:07.300
you know, businessman,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.501
but he's got an incredible

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.503
criminal background behind him.

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:12.572
So this is a dangerous group.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.307
They're quite large, are quite powerful.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.742
And there they have

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.243
at least reach

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.711
throughout parts of Europe

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:19.412
and into Africa

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.214
and maybe some parts of the Middle East.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:23.583
We ran into them in the Middle East

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.585
a couple of years ago in Syria,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.720
about a battalion sized force

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.189
that was attacking one of our positions.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:31.291
And we destroyed that force.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.125
So they are there.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.493
They're aggressive there.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:34.527
Most of them are former

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.529
Russian soldiers of one kind or another.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.697
A lot of internationals work

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:38.298
with them as well.

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.799
So very dangerous group,

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:42.068
long reach, very wealthy, very rich.

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.137
And they are probably very

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.873
disruptive, internal to Russian society.

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.942
Terminology with respect to back,

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:50.610
which you mentioned earlier,

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.811
it appears that Russia

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:53.546
is still

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.081
unable to accomplish

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.583
core strategic objectives.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.218
It is frankly remarkable to me

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:00.286
that it still stands

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:02.722
and is still owned by the Ukrainians.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:04.991
Do you share the perspective

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.860
that the failure of Russia

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.062
after going all out to capture this town

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.698
is indicative of the fact

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.632
that we're still facing

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.533
that the Ukrainians, rather,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.334
are still facing

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.368
the same

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.936
deeply incompetent military

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.705
that they were facing last year?

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.973
Or is this a special

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.074
brand of incompetence

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:21.541
that we're seeing

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:22.008
with respect

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.811
to this particular military effort?

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.646
I think the Russians are struggling

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.248
in a big way with command and control,

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:29.849
logistics, sustainment, basic

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.918
tactical doctrine, but also training.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.920
These forces are very undertrained.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:34.554
They're essentially

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:35.421
doing frontal assaults

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.823
into Machine-Gun positions, etc.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.457
They're getting slaughtered.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.491
The Russian troops are

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.359
Ukrainians are doing

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.728
a very effective area defense

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:42.829
that is proven

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.630
to be very costly

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:44.197
to the Russians

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:46.266
for about the last 20, 21 days.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.101
The Russians have not made any progress

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.003
whatsoever in and around back.

00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:50.603
So it's a slaughter

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.971
first for the Russians.

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.439
They're getting hammered in the vicinity,

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.841
but the Ukrainians have fought very,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.441
very well.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.543
That's also true

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:57.443
across the entire

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.445
front line trace from Crimean

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:01.314
all the way down to Kurdistan.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:02.182
The Ukrainians have fought

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:03.816
a remarkable defensive fight

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.485
and the Russians have not achieved

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.187
their strategic objectives.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.621
Do you see the Russian objectives

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.622
with respect to permit

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.858
as being part of their offensive?

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.693
Or would you say this is a special effort

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.394
and the broader

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.429
offensive has yet to begin?

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.031
No, I think it's the latter. I think.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.799
I think the Russian offensive,

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.901
if you will, began some time ago.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.003
And it has had fits and starts

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:24.871
and it has not achieved

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.905
the momentum and success

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:27.240
that they expected it to achieve.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.544
If I could ask you a broader question,

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:34.380
which you may not be able to answer.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.748
If we had never supported

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.051
the Ukrainians at all,

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.384
would

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.487
Russia have conquered Ukraine by now?

00:03:41.487 --> 00:03:43.456
I think without Western support?

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:43.823
First of all,

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.057
I think

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.158
the Ukrainian people

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.827
there will is indomitable.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.695
These are the same people

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:48.928
that are

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.630
the sons and grandsons of the folks

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:50.897
who fought

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:52.432
Stalin and Zhukov for ten years

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.367
from 1945 to 1955.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.169
So the Ukrainians are not going to be

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:57.904
easily conquered no matter what.

00:03:57.904 --> 00:03:59.372
If they're fighting with pitchforks

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.774
and spears, they're going to fight back.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.911
But having said that, they would have

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.480
probably lost considerably more ground

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.682
without Western assistance.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:10.817
There's no question in my mind

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:11.251
about that.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.485
So I think Western assistance

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:13.519
has been critical

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:14.387
to the Ukrainians

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.122
being able to defend themselves

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.857
with respect to Putin.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.826
Seems to me, seems to a lot of folks

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.361
very clear that he's a war criminal.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:22.428
Lots of evidence for this.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.830
And yet there are plenty of people

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.797
in this country

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:25.698
who still don't see it

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:26.766
that way, who see Putin

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.601
is basically a national leader

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.670
pursuing national interests.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.171
If you could speak to those folks

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.172
and give us your sense

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:34.874
on his status as a war criminal,

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.209
that would be appreciated.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:37.844
I think the war itself is illegal.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:40.213
It's it undermines the very

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.180
one of the first principles

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.283
that were established after World War Two

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:43.983
that underwrites

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.251
the so-called Rules-Based

00:04:45.251 --> 00:04:46.019
International Order.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.220
That is part of the United Nations,

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.555
for example, which is wars of aggression,

00:04:50.256 --> 00:04:51.424
which are unprovoked,

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.493
not in the cause of defense,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.360
where large countries

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.395
then use their military force

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:56.329
to attack smaller countries,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.131
not in the defense of their own nation.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.465
And Ukraine presented

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.634
no military threat whatsoever to Russia.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.070
And yet he lined up 100, 700

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.605
200,000 troops,

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:07.206
multiple divisions, multiplex events.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.474
And he conducted a major league war

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.142
of aggression.

00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:09.909
A war of aggression

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.844
in and of itself is a war crime.

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:12.578
And then, of course, you've

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:13.613
got the actual war crimes

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:15.048
in many of the cities and towns

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.150
When you bomb and shelled

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.217
civilian cities,

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.519
when you bomb and show

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:21.120
civilian infrastructure,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.721
when you're

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:22.989
when you're killing kids

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.290
and women and children,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.224
all of that

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.527
all of that is war, criminal war crimes.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.929
And their units, their unit commanders

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:30.630
all the way up

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.899
the chain are committing war crimes.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:34.500
The Russian forces are.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.202
And it's a tragic unfolding of events.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:37.136
But it's true.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:38.071
There's a lot of war crimes

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:38.571
being committed

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.540
by the Russian forces in Ukraine.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.641
Putin has

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:45.812
clearly made some of the most outrageous

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.280
miscalculations

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.315
of any leader in modern times.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:53.753
He miscalculated the will and commitment

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:54.687
of the Ukraine people

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.123
he made a major miscalculation

00:05:57.824 --> 00:05:59.892
in not understanding

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.728
the leadership of the U.S.

00:06:01.728 --> 00:06:03.363
and the commitment of the U.S.

00:06:03.363 --> 00:06:04.263
to lead

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:07.166
and he made another miscalculation in

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.336
not understanding how our allies,

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.171
trans-Atlantic allies in particular,

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.840
but even our global allies

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:15.208
even it beyond NATO's,

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:17.377
how they banded together

00:06:17.377 --> 00:06:18.578
so coherently

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:20.613
and strongly under this leadership.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.883
And I've been able to witness this

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.752
not only as a member of this committee,

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:27.453
both informed by classified

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.288
and public information,

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.623
but also

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:31.824
with my service

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.826
on the Foreign Affairs Committee

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.962
where I chaired and ranked

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.764
on the European subcommittee

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:40.800
for that time, engaged in very private

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.135
and important conversations

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.569
with leaders there

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.605
Yet, there are voices

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.740
in the American public right now

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.878
that will say that our coalition partners

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:53.379
are not holding up

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.381
their end of the bargain.

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:58.284
I'm informed by information.

00:06:58.284 --> 00:06:58.684
You know,

00:06:58.684 --> 00:07:00.887
I've had that just to the contrary.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:02.522
In fact, it's quite extraordinary

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:04.223
and in some areas,

00:07:04.223 --> 00:07:07.293
some countries historic in nature.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.495
But can you take this opportunity

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:11.597
to inform from your perspectives

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.333
the American public that they're wrong?

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.134
Because we have people

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.636
voicing those concerns

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:18.838
and using that as a justification to say

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:19.605
the U.S.

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:21.541
shouldn't be committed to Ukraine

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.109
because these other countries

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:23.776
aren't holding up

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:24.811
their end of the bargain

00:07:24.811 --> 00:07:26.412
when I've been informed

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:27.413
that they clearly are.

00:07:27.413 --> 00:07:29.282
But can you take this moment here

00:07:29.282 --> 00:07:29.649
in from

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:30.049
this committee

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:32.251
to just inform the American public

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:34.053
that level of commitment

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.555
that exists there,

00:07:35.555 --> 00:07:37.690
how strong it is, how important it is,

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.660
and how they are carrying great weight?

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:42.361
Well, thank you, sir.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.896
I think you're exactly right.

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.064
As you know, I meet with

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.302
50 plus nations,

00:07:49.302 --> 00:07:50.136
the ministers

00:07:50.136 --> 00:07:53.172
of defense of those nations every month.

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:54.073
And

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.577
in those meetings, what I see displayed

00:07:57.577 --> 00:08:00.213
is a strong sense of commitment and unity

00:08:00.947 --> 00:08:02.081
to support Ukraine

00:08:02.081 --> 00:08:03.182
for as long as it takes.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:03.916
As a matter of fact,

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:04.650
that's the language

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.253
that I hear them employ

00:08:07.253 --> 00:08:08.221
Some of those countries,

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:10.623
especially the smaller ones, have given

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.191
a lot in in terms

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:14.160
of the percentage of their GDP.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.229
And they're looking for ways to do more

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.297
and when they've run out of stuff,

00:08:18.297 --> 00:08:21.067
they invest money in in things

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:22.802
like helping other countries

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.504
expand their product lines.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:26.472
As as we look to acquire

00:08:26.472 --> 00:08:28.708
additional munitions and weapons.

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:31.110
So the commitment that I see is strong.

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:33.813
What I've seen them provide is

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:36.315
is is impressive.

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.684
But there's always more than we can do.

00:08:39.018 --> 00:08:40.286
And you hear me

00:08:41.287 --> 00:08:42.555
consistently beating the

00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:43.489
drum for more air

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.625
defense and other things.

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.393
In support of Ukraine.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.928
But what I've seen thus far,

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.264
I've seen tremendous support

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:53.499
for for Ukraine in helping

